.TH THUMTOO-STATUS 1 "2026-09-16" "thumtoo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
thumtoo-status \- inspect a thumtoo Store cache or one path/URI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thumtoo-status
[\fB\-\-cache\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fBsummary\fR|\fBstore\fR]
.P
.B thumtoo-status
[\fB\-\-cache\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.B path
\fIPATH\fR|\fIURI\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Report redesign Store (schema \(>= 100) contents.
.TP
.B summary
(default) Cache layout, schema version, blob/locator/media/region/tile counts.
.TP
.B path PATH|URI
Per-URI report: locator, opaque
.B mtime_ticks
(file_clock fingerprint; may be negative, not Unix nanoseconds), optional
wall-clock
.BR file_mtime ,
LQIP presence, media size, and tile pyramid coverage
(min/max scale, per-scale have/expected/missing).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache " DIR"
Cache root (default:
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumtoo
or
.IR ~/.cache/thumtoo ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
thumtoo-status
thumtoo-status path /home/me/pic.jpg
thumtoo-status path 'file:///a.rar//archive:dir/img.jpg'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thumtoo (7),
.BR thumtoo-prepare (1),
.BR thumtoo-gc (1)
